# Database Migration Workflow

This document outlines the strict protocol for evolving the `{DB_PROVIDER}` database safely.

## 1. Schema Changes
All schema mutations MUST occur in: `{SCHEMA_FILE_PATH}`
Do not manually execute DDL statements against the database.

## 2. Generating Migrations
When the schema is modified, run the following command to generate the migration file:
\`\`\`bash
{GENERATE_COMMAND}
\`\`\`

## 3. Applying Migrations
To apply the migration to your local/development database:
\`\`\`bash
{APPLY_COMMAND}
\`\`\`

## 4. CI/CD Enforcement
- Migrations MUST be committed to version control.
- In production, migrations are applied via the CI/CD pipeline using `{PROD_APPLY_COMMAND}` before the new application code is deployed.
- Never run migrations manually against production.

## 5. Seed Data
If baseline data is required (e.g. default roles, admin users), maintain the seed script in `{SEED_FILE_PATH}` and run:
\`\`\`bash
{SEED_COMMAND}
\`\`\`
